akantu-rs oracle VARIANT patch ud814 — MatrixBase::eig: zero eigenpairs after NoConvergence

NOT applied to the regular oracle builds (oracle/patches/variants/ is outside
the oracle/patches/*.patch glob of oracle/scripts/in-container/build.sh).
Applied on top of ud031-anisotropic-damage-zero-init.patch by
oracle/scripts/build-ud031-variant.sh (the "UD-031 variant" of
docs/ORACLE_BUILD.md section 12.1 carries both patches since WP-MAT-FIX5).
Upstream: akantu 35a851780d0b9471d258ed53a003ae98aaa95ea0
Defect: UD-814 (docs/UPSTREAM_DEFECTS.md, category A: undefined behaviour is
compared against a patched oracle, D-003). Akantu's
`MatrixBase::eig(values, vectors, sort)` (src/common/aka_types.hh) never
checks `EigenSolver::info()`. After `NoConvergence` (Eigen's RealSchur does
not deflate, e.g. on a 3 x 3 matrix holding NaN) `EigenSolver::compute`
writes neither `m_eivalues` nor `m_eivec` but leaves `m_eigenvectorsOk` set,
so `eig()` copies, sorts and returns the solver's uninitialised members
(fixed-size Eigen matrices on the stack). Reached by the anisotropic damage
law in 3-D once UD-763 has made the damage NaN (`tensorSqrt(1 - D)`), review
V100 MX3-01: valgrind finds 686 uninitialised reads in
variant_ud031/3d_uniaxial on a build with the UD-031 patch alone. Masked in
every recorded quantity as long as the garbage is not a NaN with a payload
(the stress is NaN through `(1 - D):sigma_el`), so the hunk changes no
recorded value; it makes the goldens independent of stack contents.
The hunk is a status check that returns zero eigenpairs, exactly what the
following code returns if the two members had been zero-initialised
(eigenvectors() of a zero `m_eivec` is zero, `normalize()` leaves a zero
column alone, the complex-eigenvector check passes, the sort of equal
values keeps the identity permutation). It only acts on NoConvergence: after
NumericalIssue the solver has written the Schur vectors and, for N <= 2,
every eigenvalue, so those defined values are left as upstream computes
them. No formula is added or changed; every converged solve is untouched.
The values-only overloads `eig()` / `eig(values)` share the defect but no
variant case reaches them with a non-converging matrix (they see the strain
and the never-written elastic stress, both finite), so they are not patched
(minimal change).
How to build: oracle/scripts/build-ud031-variant.sh (rebuilds the whole
strict library: every translation unit includes aka_types.hh). Documented
in docs/ORACLE_BUILD.md section 12.1.

--- a/src/common/aka_types.hh
+++ b/src/common/aka_types.hh
@@ -473,6 +473,13 @@
   EigenSolver<akantu::details::MapPlainObjectType_t<std::decay_t<Derived>>>
       solver(*this, true);
 
+  // akantu-rs UD-814 variant: zero eigenpairs after NoConvergence
+  if (solver.info() == Eigen::NoConvergence) {
+    values.setZero();
+    vectors.setZero();
+    return;
+  }
+
   // as advised by the Eigen developers even though this is a UB
   // auto & values = const_cast<MatrixBase<D1> &>(values_);
   // auto & vectors = const_cast<MatrixBase<D2> &>(vectors_);
